rmc-cultist-name = Xeno Cultist
rmc-cultist-objective = Allow your eligible civilian survivor to secretly serve the xenonid hive during the 10% roundstart cult event. Also requires a survivor job preference. During cult rounds, eligible survivor jobs require this preference; other survivor jobs remain ordinary survivors and do not require it. One of the selected cultists randomly becomes their leader. Your survivor equipment and skills are preserved.
rmc-cultist-greeting = You serve the hive! Obey the Queen Mother, the Queen, and your cult leader. Support the xenonids by any means, even at the cost of your life. Keep captured hosts alive. Learn the xenonid language by hearing nearby speech, just like other language learners. Knowledge is limited to 50%, and speech unlocks at 25%. Once speech is unlocked, select Xenonid in your language menu to speak to nearby characters. Unfamiliar words remain distorted. You cannot send or receive hivemind messages. Check your language menu for progress.
rmc-cultist-leader-greeting = You secretly lead the cult! Obey the Queen Mother and the Queen. Use your psychic powers to convert humans and stun enemies. Your survivor equipment and skills remain unchanged. Learn the xenonid language by hearing nearby speech, just like other language learners. Knowledge is limited to 50%, and speech unlocks at 25%. Once speech is unlocked, select Xenonid in your language menu to speak to nearby characters. Unfamiliar words remain distorted. You cannot send or receive hivemind messages. Check your language menu for progress. Keep captured hosts alive.
rmc-cultist-no-queen = There is no Queen. You are alone.
rmc-cultist-strong-mind = This mind is too strong for your powers.
rmc-cultist-stun-warning = An alien presence invades your mind. You find yourself unable to move!
rmc-cultist-stun-success = An immense psychic wave passes through you, causing you to pass out!
rmc-cultist-converted = {$cultist} has been converted into a cultist!
rmc-cultist-friendly-fire-enabled = Mutual damage with your hive is enabled. Resin doors deny you access, and weeds and sticky resin slow you down. Resin never speeds you up. Stuns and pulls still affect you.
rmc-cultist-friendly-fire-disabled = Mutual damage with your hive is disabled. Resin doors allow you access, and your hive's weeds and sticky resin do not slow you down. Resin never speeds you up. Stuns and pulls still affect you.
rmc-cultist-devotion-gained = Devotion: +{$amount}. Shared reserve: {$balance}.
rmc-cultist-rites-title = Hive Rites — Devotion {$balance}/{$capacity}
rmc-cultist-rites-help = Stay conscious and stand together.
    Nominate yourself; another cultist joins through Hive Rites.
    Voluntary transfer with the leader: {$transfer} seconds, free.
    Leader dead or absent for {$absence} minutes:
    {$succession} seconds together, or {$solitary} for the last survivor, free.
    Replace a living leader without their participation:
    {$usurpation} seconds and {$cost} Devotion, once per {$cooldown} minutes.
    Moving, damage or unconsciousness interrupts the rite.
    Devotion is spent only on success.
rmc-cultist-devotion-help = Conversion +{$conversion}; parasite trap preparation +{$trap};
    successful implantation +{$infection}; xenonid rescue +{$xeno};
    comms sabotage +{$sabotage}; biosignature sensor tower sabotage +{$sensor};
    joint sacrifice +{$sacrifice}.
    Sacrifice: choose a living, lying human through Hive Rites, then another cultist joins.
    Both must stay beside the victim for {$sacrificeDelay} seconds.
    Movement, participant damage or unconsciousness interrupts it.
    Infected hosts, cultists, xenonids and synthetics cannot be sacrificed.
    Rewards from the same target and activity have a shared {$rewardCooldown}-minute cooldown.
    Traps also reward at most once per {$trapCooldown}s per cultist.
    Sabotage: disable a working comms or biosignature sensor tower
    for {$sabotageDelay} seconds. Restoring operation cancels the timer.
    Rescue: enemy damage must reach {$damage}% of the death threshold.
    Drag the ally {$distance} tiles onto your hive's weeds, then keep
    them alive there for {$safety} seconds without further hits.
    Repeating a reward requires a new completed action after the cooldown.
    A tower left offline does not keep generating Devotion.
rmc-cultist-rites-help-button = Conditions and Devotion rewards
rmc-cultist-rites-succession-help = Succession
rmc-cultist-rites-rewards-help = Devotion
rmc-cultist-rites-back = Back to rites
rmc-cultist-rites-idle = Choose a rite, or nominate yourself and have another cultist support your succession.
rmc-cultist-rites-waiting = Candidate {$candidate} is waiting for a supporter.
rmc-cultist-rites-channeling = {$candidate} is performing a succession rite.
rmc-cultist-rite-nominate = Nominate yourself as leader
rmc-cultist-rite-support = Support candidate: {$candidate}
rmc-cultist-rite-cancel = Cancel the rite
rmc-cultist-rite-invitation = {$candidate} begins a prayer of succession. Another cultist can join through Hive Rites.
rmc-cultist-rite-started = {$candidate} performs a rite of succession. The prayer will take {$seconds} seconds.
rmc-cultist-rite-interrupted = The rite of succession was interrupted. No Devotion was spent.
rmc-cultist-rite-unavailable = Replacing a living leader requires sufficient Devotion and an expired usurpation cooldown.
rmc-cultist-rite-requirements = Stay conscious and stand beside the candidate. You cannot join while using another ability.
rmc-cultist-rite-completed = {$candidate} becomes the cult's new leader!
rmc-cultist-rite-parasite = Nurture a parasite — {$cost} Devotion
rmc-cultist-rite-parasite-description = Perform a personal {$seconds}-second rite to receive a portable capsule holding one ordinary parasite. The capsule fits inside a bag and preserves its occupant. Open the lid, then take the parasite out; click a living, lying or nested host with it to begin the normal two-second attachment. Helmets, masks and infection resistance retain their normal effects. Devotion is spent only on success.
rmc-cultist-parasite-rite-started = You begin nurturing a parasite. Stay still for {$seconds} seconds.
rmc-cultist-parasite-rite-interrupted = The nurturing rite was interrupted. No Devotion was spent.
rmc-cultist-parasite-rite-unavailable = Stay conscious and finish your current ability. The rite requires {$cost} shared Devotion.
rmc-cultist-parasite-rite-completed = You receive a parasite capsule for {$cost} Devotion. Shared reserve: {$balance}.
rmc-cultist-parasite-slot = Parasite
rmc-cultist-parasite-capsule-opened = The capsule's lid is open.
rmc-cultist-parasite-capsule-closed = The capsule is closed. Open its lid first.
rmc-cultist-rite-sacrifice = Joint sacrifice
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-description = Choose a living, lying human and have another cultist join through Hive Rites. Both must remain beside the victim for {$seconds} seconds. The victim is torn apart, granting up to {$reward} shared Devotion. Moving, damage to either participant, unconsciousness or loss of reach interrupts the rite. Infected hosts, cultists, xenonids and synthetics are excluded.
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-offer = Prepare sacrifice: {$victim}
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-join = Join sacrifice of {$victim}
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-cancel = Cancel the sacrifice
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-invitation = {$cultist} prepares a sacrifice over {$victim}. Another cultist must join through Hive Rites.
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-started = {$first} and {$second} begin tearing {$victim} apart! The rite will take {$seconds} seconds.
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-unavailable = The rite requires two available cultists of the same hive beside a living, lying, uninfected human. Finish any other rite first.
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-interrupted = The sacrifice was interrupted. No Devotion was earned.
rmc-cultist-sacrifice-completed = {$victim} has been sacrificed to the hive!
ent-RMCActionCultistRites = Hive Rites
    .desc = View shared Devotion, nurture a parasite, perform a joint sacrifice or arrange a succession rite.
